  "summary_plain": "Fifty-three printed regions on two pages. Both staves open in treble and bass, with four sharps and cut time, and no later clef or meter change is printed. The first region is a one-quarter pickup; every later region is a complete cut-time bar. A double bar after the twenty-fifth region carries a courtesy change to one sharp, reprinted under the Intermezzo heading on the next system. A double bar after the fortieth region carries a courtesy return to four sharps, reprinted on the following system. Neither double bar has repeat dots. The last region ends with a thin-and-thick final barline and is a full bar, so the pickup is not balanced by a shortened close.",
